bilbo recall: search what bilbo keeps and print the chunks that match best.

[1mUsage:[22m
  [36mbilbo recall [39m[2m<query>[22m[36m... [--in [39m[2m<label>[22m[36m]... [--kind [39m[2m<kind>[22m[36m]...[39m
               [--budget [2m<tokens>[22m]

[1mOptions:[22m
      [1m--in [22m[2m<label>[22m       Search what a label or an id names; repeat it for more
      [1m--kind [22m[2m<kind>[22m      Search entries of this kind only; repeat it for more
      [1m--budget [22m[2m<tokens>[22m  Print at most this many tokens

[1mOutput:[22m
  [1m=== [22m[2m<ref>[22m[1m [22m[2m<n>[22m[1m lines[22m   a hit's header (tab-separated), then [2m<n>[22m lines of text
  [1m... part [22m[2m<k>[22m[1m/[22m[2m<m>[22m      one piece of a record too long for a chunk
  [1m... cut[22m               the last hit, cut to fit the budget
  [2m<ref>[22m                 bilbo read takes it: the end of the id and the records
  [1mqueries.log[22m           in the state folder: each query that reaches the store
[2m--in takes an id, whole or as a hit prints it, or words of a label (bilbo read[22m
[2m<id> lists labels). A value that starts with - takes =: --in=-home-me-src-shed[22m

[1mExit:[22m
  [1m0[22m  at least one hit
  [1m1[22m  nothing matched, no store, no search index, or a store or index failure
  [1m2[22m  usage or config error

[1mExamples:[22m
  [36mbilbo recall how did we decide the index format[39m
  [36mbilbo recall --in bilbo --in notes --budget 1500 -- release checklist[39m

[1mDocs:[22m [2mhttps://github.com/delucca/bilbo/wiki/Commands#recall[22m
